","huwiki-text-en":"! Music articles · read, listen and try

Music articles can do more than display a picture. Play a short score excerpt within the explanation, select notes and open the whole tune afterwards.

!! Start here

* 🎻 [[Swedish polka – melody, pulse and ensemble|Musikartikel – Svensk polka]] · 2/4, alternating bass, accordion offbeats and short examples from ''Silbaätno''.
* 🎷 [[Swing and walking bass – from two-feel to four-feel|Musikartikel – Jazz 2-feel og walking]] · excerpts from the same AABA study.

!! Explore more styles

* [[Folk music|HUWiki Musikmodul – folk]] · Irish jigs, Nordic dances and polka
* [[Jazz|HUWiki Musikmodul – jazz]] · swing, AABA, walking and bossa
* [[Balkan|HUWiki Musikmodul – balkan]] · 7/8, 9/8 and 11/8
* [[India|HUWiki Musikmodul – india]] · raga, drone and konnakol
* [[Rhythm|HUWiki Musikmodul – rhythm]] · clave, samba and syncopation

!! How excerpts work

This macro selects just written bars 3–6 of the bundled jig:

```
<<abc-example "HUWiki ABC – Eksempel: Jig" bars:"3-6">>
```

The excerpt retains the applicable clef, key, meter and tempo. Set `audio:"no"` for a silent notation illustration or `show-title:"yes"` to display the score title. Changes to the original score appear in the article automatically.

[[More advanced macro examples|HUWiki ABC – Nodeeksempler]] · [[Music Edition|HUWiki Musik – Start]]

